+# 🧭 SCOUT RADAR IV — 2026-10-28 (Provider-Depth Sweep — Routing Supply & Catalog Ingest)
+
+> **Role:** Ecosystem Scout · **Job:** 478344 · **Cycle:** single-dispatch · **Doctrine:** high-signal
+> only (per #1658). Every signal below was **live-probed on 2026-10-28** before filing; each issue
+> carries dated evidence, a smallest-safe-slice proposal mapped to named files already on `main`,
+> acceptance criteria, and a never-do register.
+> **Non-duplication:** R1–R12 (landed #1611) covered model families, MCP 2026-07-28 spec, ALMA,
+> DualPath, eval studies, Anthropic risk disclosures. R13–R16 (landed #1652) covered payments
+> (x402), observability (OTel GenAI), agent↔agent protocol (A2A), execution isolation (Firecracker).
+> R17–R20 (landed #1682) covered the Agent Skills standard, chrome-devtools-mcp, sigstore
+> attestation provenance, and Web Bot Auth. This radar scans the lane all three deliberately
+> deferred: **routing supply depth** — which concrete OpenAI-compatible provider endpoints the
+> dynamic router can actually reach today — and the **catalog ingest lane** — public, versioned
+> server catalogs the marketplace can ingest verbatim. Task ID renamed `…radar-iv` after the
+> landed #1682 claimed `…radar-iii` mid-cycle (filename collision caught at rebase; zero content
+> overlap between the two sweeps).
