+## 2. Full-Spectrum Evaluations
+
+### R21 · Routing supply: four live provider lanes the router cannot reach — `adapt_cleanroom`
+
+**Evidence trail (all probed 2026-10-28):**
+
+| Provider | Probe | Result | Doc anchor |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| Z.ai (GLM) | `POST https://api.z.ai/api/paas/v4/chat/completions` `{}` | **HTTP 401** | `docs.z.ai/guides/llm/glm-4.6` — base `https://api.z.ai/api/paas/v4/`; `glm-4.6` + GLM-5.x family; coding plans from $18/mo |
+| DashScope intl (Qwen) | `POST https://dashscope-intl.aliyuncs.com/compatible-mode/v1/chat/completions` `{}` | **HTTP 400** (protocol-level validation error = endpoint live) | `alibabacloud.com/help/en/model-studio/compatibility-of-openai-with-dashscope` — compatible-mode; `qwen3.8-max`, `qwen-plus`; docs note workspace-scoped migration, legacy domain still serving |
+| Mistral | `POST https://api.mistral.ai/v1/chat/completions` `{}` | **HTTP 401** | OpenAI-compatible `/v1`; `gateway/model_horizon.json` already tracks `mistral/mistral-large-latest` |
+| Cerebras | `POST https://api.cerebras.ai/v1/chat/completions` `{}` | **HTTP 403** (WAF pre-auth = live) | `inference-docs.cerebras.ai/models/overview` — `gpt-oss-120b`, `qwen-3.8-27b`; $5 trial credit; shared-inference free tier |
+
+**Internal drift proof:** the routing brain's knowledge file (`model_horizon.json`) lists mistral
+as a model family, but `gateway/services/dynamic_ai/provider_registry.py` has no mistral template —
+knowledge exists that routing cannot act on. The only `qwen` presence is inside the `bai` router
+aggregate (lines 195–196), not a direct lane. Z.ai and Cerebras: zero presence anywhere.
+
+- **Pros:** each lane is one data-only template block in `ProviderRegistry.initialize()` —
+  the registry's own doctrine is "keys come from environment!" (`_validate_api_key`,
+  `refresh_status`, availability gating are already generic and fail-closed); directly widens
+  failover diversity for the dynamic router and the P-01/P-10 cost-routing lanes; Mistral closes
+  a live knowledge-vs-routing mismatch, not a hypothetical one.
+- **Cons:** four more providers to health-monitor; free-tier claims differ (Cerebras trial tier vs
+  paid-only Mistral) and must not distort the free-first priority ordering.
+- **Risks:** endpoint drift (DashScope is mid-migration to workspace-scoped hosts — the issue pins
+  the legacy compatible-mode host that probed live, with the doc-noted successor recorded);
+  priority inflation tempting solvers to place paid lanes above free tiers.
+- **এটা করা যাবে না:** no hardcoded keys; no per-provider request-mutation hacks (OpenAI-compatible
+  means the shared client path stays shared); no free-tier priority inversion.
+- **Adoption path → Issue [#1685](https://github.com/Supremeai-bd/supremeai-open/issues/1685)**
+  (Parent Anchor Hub #750): four templates, env keys (`ZAI_API_KEY`, `DASHSCOPE_API_KEY`,
+  `MISTRAL_API_KEY`, `CEREBRAS_API_KEY`), model IDs pinned from the dated doc anchors above.
+
+### R22 · Catalog ingest: the official MCP Registry as a marketplace source — `accept_verbatim` (read-only ingest)
+
+**Evidence trail (probed 2026-10-28):** `GET https://registry.modelcontextprotocol.io/v0.1/ping` →
+`{"pong":true}` HTTP 200; `GET /v0.1/servers?limit=1` → HTTP 200, paginated (`servers[]` +
+`metadata`), records self-describing via `$schema: https://static.modelcontextprotocol.io/schemas/
+2025-12-11/server.schema.json` with `remotes[].type: "streamable-http"` observed live; API docs at
+`/docs`. This is the MCP project's own public catalog of remote servers — versioned, schema'd,
+machine-readable.
+
+**Federation seam (on `main` today):** discovery is strictly one-by-one —
+`gateway/routes/mcp_marketplace.py::discover_mcp_server` + Tower `client_register_mcp_server` /
+`client_discover_mcp_server`. WO #1523 (mcp_plugins registry + one-click BYO connect) is queued
+with no external catalog source. Users must already know a server URL to connect.
+
+- **Pros:** read-only ingest with zero new runtime dependency (plain HTTP + existing
+  `connection_registry`); `streamable-http` filter maps exactly onto the transport the tower
+  client speaks (fail-closed on SSE-only records); turns WO #1523's "one-click connect" from
+  a form into a browsable catalog.
+- **Cons:** catalog quality is upstream's (descriptions/titles vary); pagination volume needs a
+  cache-first design; `$schema` versions will advance (2025-12-11 today).
+- **Risks:** bulk auto-registration would import untrusted endpoints — must stay
+  human-approved-per-connection; stale rows after upstream churn.
+- **এটা করা যাবে না:** no auto-registration, no credential handling in the sync path, no HTML
+  scraping where a public JSON API exists.
+- **Adoption path → Issue [#1686](https://github.com/Supremeai-bd/supremeai-open/issues/1686)**
+  (Parent Anchor Hub #753, synergy WO #1523): cache-first sync adapter, normalized rows
+  (`name/title/description/version/remotes[]/schemaVersion`), one-click prefill of
+  `discover_mcp_server()` payloads.
