+## 3. Cross-Signal Synthesis
+
+R21 and R22 are the same story from two sides: **supply**. R21 widens what the router can *reach*
+(model inference supply), R22 widens what the marketplace can *offer* (tool supply). Both are
+data-only integrations against live, versioned, protocol-stable surfaces — no new dependencies,
+no adapter code beyond one template block / one sync function each, and both respect the
+free-first priority and human-approval trust boundaries already on main. Sequence: R21 first
+(routing resilience is load-bearing today; the mistral horizon mismatch is a live inconsistency),
+R22 second (rides on WO #1523 landing its schema first).
+
